    "task_id": "batch-execution-recovery-s2-failure-recovery",
    "goal": "Make batch failure recovery reflect fresh Kernel obligations and findings, and expose safe check diagnostics so repair, finding disposition and fresh Assurance lead to settlement without redundant human approval.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "BER-S2-A1",
        "assertion": "Meet S2 in docs/specs/batch-execution-recovery.spec.md: both Hosts return the fresh Kernel obligation and specific task/acceptance/finding identities with one legal recovery action. Ordinary own-claim technical repair is not presented as user authorization, unchanged QA is not retried blindly, environment failures remain distinct, and local green cannot settle a task with open findings. Behavioral tests exercise repair, verified finding disposition, fresh deterministic QA and required Review before settlement. QA diagnostics contain only bounded allowlisted descriptor identity, phase/outcome/timing and byte-count metadata; injected raw stdout/stderr and secret-bearing arguments/environment values never enter reports, findings, TaskRecord, audit or tracker evidence.",
