      "acceptance_id": "BER-S2-A1",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 1,
      "summary": "Review 准备失败仍被误报为需要用户决策：coordinator.ts:284-308 未为 review_preparation_failed 推导恢复动作，Claude kernel_ports.ts:1222 将其压成 failed，batch_runner.ts:1182-1199 随后把仍持有自身 claim 的 child 停泊为 needs_human，并要求重新确认。应保留这一失败分类，返回携带 fresh run_review 身份的技术修复动作，维持 running/enrolled，修复后仅恢复 Review，不重跑已提交 QA；补充两 Host 的回归测试。",
      "anchor": "sha256:c45465a871d706c0dd98489985a9e6aca3dfa06ca97c26394163de505bee6fa3",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "Invariant class: recoverable own-claim Assurance failures must retain their actual obligation rather than become user-authorization requests. A material child has fresh committed QA, frozen artifacts, next_obligation=run_review, valid batch authorization, no open findings or user decisions, and no surviving Review reservation after interruption. During start_unattended_batch continuation, buildAssurance(review) or writeReviewEvidence fails, for example because the temporary evidence directory cannot be created. advanceOnce returns review_preparation_failed, but the added recovery derivation recognizes only finding repair, QA environment_failure and authorization cases, so it returns null for this class. Both batch paths then reach the generic park branch; Claude additionally erases review_preparation_failed into failed. The QA-environment and Review-finding handling added in this revision does not cover read-only Review preparation failures. The resulting report lacks the fresh run_review recovery identity and says a human decision/re-confirmation is required although Kernel QA remains valid and no new authorization is needed.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_runner.ts:resumeBatch",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_runner.ts:driveInterruptedChild",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts:createBatchKernelPort.advanceTask",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/assurance/coordinator.ts:AssuranceCoordinator.advanceOnce",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/assurance/coordinator.ts:AssuranceCoordinator.withRecovery",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/assurance/coordinator.ts:deriveAssuranceRecovery"
        ],
        "violated": {
